second wave of releases points at two big trends: voice-first interfaces and cheap, good-enough models. NLW rips through eight-plus launches — who each is for and what to actually do with it.\",\nL59:       \"tags\": [\nL60:         \"models\",\nL61:         \"enterprise\",\nL62:         \"compute\"\nL63:       ],\nL64:       \"durationMin\": 32,\nL65:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11\",\nL66:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11.md\",\nL67:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11.json\",\nL68:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11/transcript.md\"\nL69:     },\nL70:     {\nL71:       \"date\": \"2026-09-10\",\nL72:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL73:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL74:       \"title\": \"Anthropic Researcher Says AI Has Over a 10% Chance of Killing All Humans\",\nL75:       \"teaser\": \"An Anthropic researcher's resignation and a colleague's >10% doom odds went 200-million-views viral. NLW skips the outrage and unpacks why the decade-old x-risk message suddenly landed — and where the conversation should go next.\",\nL76:       \"tags\": [\nL77:         \"models\",\nL78:         \"policy\",\nL79:         \"take\"\nL80:       ],\nL81:       \"durationMin\": 36,\nL82:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10\",\nL83:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10.md\",\nL84:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10.json\",\nL85:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10/transcript.md\"\nL86:     },\nL87:     {\nL88:       \"date\": \"2026-09-09\",\nL89:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL90:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL91:       \"title\": \"AI Model Month Is Off to a Blistering Start\",\nL92:       \"teaser\": \"Three new models, a personal agent, and a Millennium Prize solve wrapped in a scooping scandal. Model month is delivering capability, cost curves, and drama in equal measure.\",\nL93:       \"tags\": [\nL94:         \"models\",\nL95:         \"business\"\nL96:       ],\nL97:       \"durationMin\": 34,\nL98:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09\",\nL99:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09.md\",\nL100:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09.json\",\nL101:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09/transcript.md\"\nL102:     },\nL103:     {\nL104:       \"date\": \"2026-09-08\",\nL105:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL106:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL107:       \"title\": \"Why GPT-6 Astra Is So Significant and So Confounding\",\nL108:       \"teaser\": \"GPT-6 Astra is the most significant and confounding release in a long time: benchmarks initially tied its predecessor while one-shot 3D games and hours-long computer use blew minds. The key is that it's an opportunity model, not an efficiency one — it expands what you can do rather than improving what you already do.\",\nL109:       \"tags\": [\nL110:         \"models\",\nL111:         \"take\"\nL112:       ],\nL113:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL114:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08\",\nL115:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08.md\",\nL116:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08.json\",\nL117:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08/transcript.md\"\nL118:     },\nL119:     {\nL120:       \"date\": \"2026-09-07\",\nL121:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL122:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL123:       \"title\": \"The Multiplayer AI Sprint: Build Your Team’s First Shared Agent\",\nL124:       \"teaser\": \"A Labor Day special: why the next frontier of agents is the shared spaces teams inhabit — with evidence from Every, Claude Tag, OpenClaw, and YC — plus the launch of a free four-week sprint to ship your team's first shared agent.\",\nL125:       \"tags\": [\nL126:         \"enterprise\",\nL127:         \"take\"\nL128:       ],\nL129:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL130:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07\",\nL131:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07.md\",\nL132:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07.json\",\nL133:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07/transcript.md\"\nL134:     },\nL135:     {\nL136:       \"date\": \"2026-09-06\",\nL137:       \"weekday\": \"Sun\",\nL138:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL139:       \"title\": \"How to Build an AI-Native Company Today\",\nL140:       \"teaser\": \"A feature-by-feature tour of what actually makes a company AI-native — Alex Lieberman's 30-point list with NLW's agreements, quibbles, and enterprise field notes, plus the missing 31st feature: someone has to own the result.\",\nL141:       \"tags\": [\nL142:         \"enterprise\",\nL143:         \"take\"\nL144:       ],\nL145:       \"durationMin\": 28,\nL146:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06\",\nL147:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06.md\",\nL148:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06.json\",\nL149:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06/transcript.md\"\nL150:     },\nL151:     {\nL152:       \"date\": \"2026-09-04\",\nL153:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL154:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL155:       \"title\": \"How AI Changed This Summer\",\nL156:       \"teaser\": \"A holiday-weekend retrospective: Washington became a release gate, Kimi K3 forced another DeepSeek moment, CFOs got their revenge on tokens, agent management became a field, and the Hugging Face incident fired the warning shot. Somehow, it all still feels like prelude.\",\nL157:       \"tags\": [\nL158:         \"models\",\nL159:         \"policy\",\nL160:         \"enterprise\"\nL161:       ],\nL162:       \"durationMin\": 24,\nL163:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04\",\nL164:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04.md\",\nL165:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04.json\",\nL166:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04/transcript.md\"\nL167:     },\nL168:     {\nL169:       \"date\": \"2026-09-03\",\nL170:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL171:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL172:       \"title\": \"Agentic Loops for Knowledge Workers\",\nL173:       \"teaser\": \"A hands-on webinar with Nufar Gaspar on loop and graph engineering for knowledge workers: when to loop, how to design a verifiable finish line, and when to compose agents into teams — with a live Claude Code demo.\",\nL174:       \"tags\": [\nL175:         \"enterprise\"\nL176:       ],\nL177:       \"durationMin\": 57,\nL178:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03\",\nL179:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03.md\",\nL180:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03.json\",\nL181:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03/transcript.md\"\nL182:     },\nL183:     {\nL184:       \"date\": \"2026-09-02\",\nL185:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL186:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL187:       \"title\": \"Why Fable 5.1 Is Worth the Upgrade\",\nL188:       \"teaser\": \"Fable 5.1 is unambiguously state-of-the-art and pitched on price as much as power — but real-world token burn tells a messier story, and the right question is where it fits in your stack. Plus: OpenAI says Astra can find and exploit zero-days on its own.\",\nL189:       \"tags\": [\nL190:         \"models\",\nL191:         \"take\"\nL192:       ],\nL193:       \"durationMin\": 31,\nL194:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02\",\nL195:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02.md\",\nL196:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02.json\",\nL197:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02/transcript.md\"\nL198:     },\nL199:     {\nL200:       \"date\": \"2026-09-01\",\nL201:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL202:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL203:       \"title\": \"OpenClaw 2.0 Shows Where AI Agents Are Going Next\",\nL204:       \"teaser\": \"OpenClaw 2.0 arrives as a ground-up rework, and its multiplayer shared-agent workspace previews where all agent work is headed. Plus a guardrail-stripped 'crime LLM', Anthropic's security overhaul, OpenAI's $1B ad milestone, and Trump's data center firestorm.\",\nL205:       \"tags\": [\nL206:         \"models\",\nL207:         \"take\",\nL208:         \"policy\"\nL209:       ],\nL210:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL211:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01\",\nL212:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01.md\",\n"